{
  "query": "An online learning platform at example.com needs a highly scalable workflow where instructors upload videos that are then transcoded to multiple bitrates, watermarked with the brand, and indexed so viewers can search by content. Upload volume is unpredictable with some days having only a few 300 MB files and other days receiving several hundred assets up to 8 GB each. The team wants a serverless design that scales automatically and minimizes operations. Which approach should they implement on Google Cloud?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Use Cloud Functions to react to new uploads in Cloud Storage, process videos with custom FFmpeg containers on Cloud Run for transcoding and watermarking, and index metadata in Elasticsearch running on Compute Engine",
      "explanation": "This design uses event driven serverless components for processing while relying on a self managed search cluster for indexing",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Use Cloud Storage for uploads, Cloud Video Intelligence API for searchable metadata, and Compute Engine managed instance groups for transcoding and watermarking",
      "explanation": "This approach stores the media and extracts labels with a managed API while scaling virtual machines to run custom encoders",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Use Cloud Storage for intake, Cloud Pub/Sub to fan out processing jobs, Cloud Dataflow to handle video transcoding and watermark overlay, and Video Intelligence API to extract labels for search",
      "explanation": "This pattern connects messaging with an autoscaling pipeline for processing and uses a managed API to generate metadata for discovery",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Implement Cloud Dataprep for video processing, use Cloud Vision API for watermark tasks, and load metadata to BigQuery for search",
      "explanation": "This proposes a data preparation service and an image analysis API with a data warehouse to support search",
      "correct": false,
