  "originalQuery": "A media company needs to build a scalable video processing system that allows content creators to upload videos, which are then transcoded, watermarked, and made searchable within their platform. The system should be able to scale automatically to accommodate varying upload frequencies and sizes. What is the best approach to implement this system?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Use Cloud Storage for video uploads, Cloud Video Intelligence API for searchable metadata, and Compute Engine for transcoding and watermarking.<br/>B. Utilize Cloud Storage for uploads, Cloud Pub/Sub for messaging, Cloud Dataflow for video processing, and Video Intelligence API for metadata.<br/>C. Implement Cloud Dataprep for video processing, Cloud Vision API for adding watermarks, and BigQuery for video searchability.<br/>D. Deploy Cloud Functions to trigger video processing, use Cloud Dataflow for transcoding and watermarking, and ElasticSearch on Compute Engine for searchability.",
